{"files": [{"path": "CWE401_Memory_Leak__malloc_realloc_int_01.c", "content": "#include "std_testcase.h"

#include <wchar.h>


void CWE401_Memory_Leak__malloc_realloc_int_01_bad()
{
    {
        int * data = (int *)malloc(100*sizeof(int));
        if (data == NULL) {exit(-1);}

        data[0] = 5;
        printIntLine(data[0]);

        {
            int *tmp = (int *)realloc(data, (130000)*sizeof(int));
            if (tmp != NULL)
            {
                data = tmp;
                data[0] = 10;
                printIntLine(data[0]);
            }
            free(data);
        }
    }
}
"}], "explanation": "The original code overwrote the only pointer to the malloc'd block with the realloc result; if realloc failed (returning NULL), the original block leaked. The fix stores realloc's result in a temporary, only replacing data on success, and always frees the still-valid pointer, preserving the same printed output and behavior."}
